\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I bind unto myself to-day
\par The strong Name of the Trinity,
\par By invocation of the same,
\par The Three in One, and One in Three.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I bind this day to me for ever,
\par By power of faith, Christ's Incarnation;
\par His baptism in the Jordan river;
\par His death on Cross for my salvation;
\par His bursting from the spiced tomb;
\par His riding up the heavenly way;
\par His coming at the day of doom:
\par I bind unto myself to-day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I bind unto myself to-day
\par The virtues of the star-lit heaven,
\par The glorious sun's life-giving ray,
\par The whiteness of the moon at even,
\par The flashing of the lightning free,
\par The whirling wind's tempestuous  shocks,
\par The stable earth, the deep  salt sea,
\par Around the old eternal rocks.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I bind unto myself to-day
\par The power of God to hold and lead,
\par His eyes to wrath, His might to stay,
\par His ear to hearken to my need,
\par The wisdom of my God to teach,
\par His hand to guide, His shield to ward,
\par The word of God to give me speech,
\par His heavenly host to be my guard.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Christ be with me, Christ within me,
\par Christ behind me, Christ before me,
\par Christ beside me, Christ to win me,
\par Christ to comfort and restore me,
\par Christ beneath me, Christ above me,
\par Christ in quiet, Christ in danger,
\par Christ in hearts of all that love me,
\par Christ in mouth of friend and stranger.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I bind  unto myself the Name,
\par The strong Name of the Trinity,
\par By invocation of the same,
\par The Three in One, and One in Three,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Of whom all nature hath creation,
\par Eternal Father, Spirit, Word.
\par Praise to the Lord of my salvation:
\par Salvation is of Christ the Lord.
\par                                    Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
